# A CANDIDATE: THE SPEECH PORT READS A LANGUAGE TAG (operator, 2026-11-25,
# relayed by München: "the language/country tag must be aligned to the
# language to speak, otherwise the voice has always a thick italian accent").
# d658549772ca's series (engine-page), line for line, then:
#   0022  OmniVoice: "it-IT", "en_GB", "IT" are the language of their first
#         subtag, where they were read as NO language, in silence; a language
#         the model does not name is said in the log; the request's summary
#         line ends with the language spoken.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-lang.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again. It touches the speech port's
# request path only (tools/mtmd/mtmd-helper-gen.cpp, one new header): no
# encoder computes anything else under it, and the gate is what says so.
# IF d658549772ca IS NOT GATED YET, this one can be gated in its place - one
# gating for the paging default and the tag (RULE 1) - or it rides the park
# engine, whose series starts from these lines.
